GOTALK 
======

GoTalk is a robust, real-time group chat application built with Go (Golang) 
and pure JavaScript. It features a WebSocket-based server, a responsive web 
client, and a terminal user interface (TUI).

KEY FEATURES
----------------

* REAL-TIME MESSAGING: Instant message delivery using WebSockets.
* MESSAGE PERSISTENCE: SQLite-backed storage ensures chat history is saved.
* CHRONOLOGICAL HISTORY: Automatically loads the last 50 messages when joining.
* EASY JOIN QR CODES: Scan terminal output or share in-app codes to join rooms.
* RESPONSIVE MOBILE UI: Fully optimized interface for mobile and desktop.
* NETWORK AUTO-DISCOVERY: Shows your local network IP for easy sharing.
* LIVE USER LIST: See who is currently online in real-time.
* ROBUST RECONNECTION: Automatic reconnection with exponential backoff.
* SECURE BY DEFAULT: Strict input validation and CORS policies.

QUICK START
------------

PREREQUISITES:
- Go 1.22 or higher
- Make (optional)

INSTALLATION:
1. Clone the repository:
   $ git clone https://github.com/udaykiriti/Gotalk.git
   $ cd Gotalk

2. Build the project:
   $ go build -o gotalk.exe ./cmd/server

RUNNING THE SERVER:
Start the server:
   $ ./gotalk.exe

The server will automatically display a SCANABLE QR CODE for your local network.

Visit http://localhost:8080 in your browser to start chatting.
Invite others by clicking the "Invite" button in the web header.

PROJECT STRUCTURE
-----------------

- cmd/server: Main server entry point (with IP detection & QR scan).
- cmd/client: TUI client entry point.
- internal/storage: SQLite persistence layer.
- internal/ws: WebSocket logic (Hub, Client, Message).
- internal/handlers: HTTP handlers.
- web: Frontend assets (Responsive HTML/CSS/JS).
- gotalk.db: SQLite database file (created automatically).

FOR MORE DETAILED DOCUMENTATION, SEE THE docs/ DIRECTORY.


